# music-ratings — build-time configuration
#
# Every value here is PUBLIC. This app has no server and no secrets.
# A Spotify client secret is never used, never required, and must never be added.
#
# You do not need this file. The build ships a working Spotify and Microsoft
# application ID (see `src/lib/config.ts`), so signing in works out of the box
# and nobody has to register anything. Use these variables only to point a build
# at *different* applications. An empty value means "not supplied", and the
# build's own ID is used; to ship with no identity at all, empty the constants
# in `src/lib/config.ts`.
#
# Whatever is set here is still overridable per user in Settings.

# --- Spotify -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Client ID from https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard (create an app, choose
# "Web API", and add the redirect URI below to the app's Redirect URIs list).
# Authorization Code with PKCE is used, so no client secret exists.
# Spotify's development mode authorises only a handful of accounts, each added
# by hand in the dashboard.
VITE_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=

# Must match a Redirect URI registered on the Spotify app *exactly*.
# Leave blank to use the app's own origin + base path at runtime.
# Example for local dev: http://127.0.0.1:5173/callback
VITE_SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_URI=

# --- Microsoft / OneDrive (optional sync) ------------------------------------
# Application (client) ID of an Azure AD app registration with a
# "Single-page application" redirect URI equal to your deployed origin + /callback.
# Register it for "any organizational directory and personal Microsoft accounts"
# so an ordinary consumer OneDrive can sign in without an administrator.
#
# No API permissions need configuring: scopes are requested at sign-in. The app
# asks for Files.ReadWrite.AppFolder and User.Read for the sandboxed app folder,
# and Files.ReadWrite instead when the user chooses their own folder.
VITE_ONEDRIVE_CLIENT_ID=

# --- Deployment --------------------------------------------------------------
# Base public path. "/" for a custom domain, "/<repo>/" for GitHub Pages
# project sites.
VITE_BASE_PATH=/
